   "text": "Added BEFORE any pilot or panel profile finished (training still running), after a scratch smoke run (work/, not a result) showed P1 opening AA ~0.58 and JJ ~0.24 in the 24-hand game, so that the responses to P1's bet are ON path and the declared scan can only meet rare own-unreached sets.  New declared experiments: (PC1) positive control: the same off-path scan applied to exact SGS family profiles of the bridge game must recover Kuhn's known poles (a11/a21 at c33 = 1/2 - b32, a41 at the upper end); (PC2) DCFR on the bridge game, 3 seeds x 30,000 iterations, analysed like the pilot; (OP2) imposed P1 silence on the 24-hand game: CFR (DCFR, seeds 1-3, 12,000 iterations) with P1's opening fixed to check, then the 72 unreached responses to a P1 bet are chosen explicitly by a deterministic deterrence search (minimise P1's full-game residual by exact coordinate minimisation, 5 declared starts), then theta = P3's KK call at B:1-F (the c33 analogue) is swept with everything else fixed and the P1 JJ-bet deviation (the a11 analogue) is measured.  OP2 is exploratory: its search gives an upper bound on the best achievable deterrence, not a proof that deterrence is impossible.",
